  "id": "t2-secant-v4",
  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "In t2-secant-v2 (readout-d1539c52c610cf0b249ed2e5) and t2-secant-v3 (readout-2dc35b433395cd50fadc41b9), reconstructing 2D ||nabla_x D||_2 from 1 tangent per sample paired across spatial neighbors left slight cross-mode slope distortion on model_ae_gan_multimodal (component_center_rms_sigma 1.0627 / 1.0778 vs <= 1.0), while fd_delta=1e-3 crossed occasional ReLU kinks on EmulatedPrecisionLinear in precision_gaussian_fp32 (cdf_ks=0.0582 vs <= 0.05). Because d <= 4 has at most 4 coordinate axes, evaluating all M = d canonical basis tangents in one stacked forward-mode AD pass eliminates spatial neighbor approximation error identically (0.000000 error vs exact gradient norm) with zero autograd.grad and zero create_graph=True double-backprop, while fd_delta=1e-4 prevents kink impulses on emulated-precision linear layers.",
